# Curator ownership.
#
# src/content/config/signoffs.json is the authority behind the review gate. The `reviewer`
# field inside a judge record is self-reported and an automated process can type
# any name into it, so the gate checks this ledger instead. That indirection is
# worth nothing unless the ledger sits somewhere a writer with access to
# src/content cannot reach, which is what this file and the "Require review from
# Code Owners" branch rule accomplish together.
#
# The same reasoning covers the gate script, the signing script, the CI
# definition that runs them, and the noindex header that keeps forty-three
# unfinished pages out of Google. Each is a control that an ordinary content
# change has no business editing.
#
# To require curator review on every change rather than only on the control
# surfaces, add a line reading:  *  @jrm2026

/src/content/config/signoffs.json    @jrm2026
/src/content/config/poison-list.json @jrm2026
/scripts/validate.mjs                @jrm2026
/scripts/gates-compliance.mjs        @jrm2026
/scripts/sign-record.mjs             @jrm2026
/.github/                            @jrm2026
/public/_headers                     @jrm2026
